(2*0=1, 2*1=0, 2*2=2). So operation is right projection except for row2 swapped for first two columns.\n\nWe need to test Eq1 for all assignments. Let\'s brute think.\n\nWe need to compute RHS = (x * (x * (y*y))) * z.\n\nFirst compute y*y = y (since for rows 0,1 it\'s right projection, for row2: 2*2=2, also right projection). So y*y = y.\n\nThen compute x * (y*y) = x * y = y (since right projection unless x=2? Wait right projection means result = second argument y, regardless of first, except when first=2? Actually row2 column y: if y=0 => 1, if y=1 =>0, if y=2=>2. So not always y. So need case analysis.\n\nLet\'s compute x*y according to table:\n\nIf x=0 or 1: result = y.\n\nIf x=2: result = swap: if y=0 =>1, y=1=>0, y=2=>2.\n\nNow compute x * (x * (y*y)). First compute inner = x*y as above, call t.\n\nNow compute x * t.\n\nAgain apply same rule.\n\nWe need to evaluate for all x,y.\n\nLet\'s enumerate possibilities.\n\nCase x=0:\n\n- x*y = y. Then x * t = 0 * y = y (since row0). So x*(x*(y*y)) = y.\n\nRHS = y * z = (since left operand y). If y=0 or1: result = z (right projection). If y=2: row2 column z: if z=0 =>1, z=1=>0, z=2=>2.\n\nThus RHS depends on y and z.\n\nEquation requires x (=0) = RHS for all y,z. For y=0, RHS = z, need 0 = z for all z, fails. So Eq1 fails.\n\nThus J not candidate.\n\nTable K: "band" maybe idempotent and associative? Table [[0,0,0],[1,1,0],[2,0,2]] rows 0,1,2.\n\nLet\'s write operation:\n\nRow0: 0*0=0,0*1=0,0*2=0.\n\nRow1: 1*0=1,1*1=1,1*2=0.\n\nRow2: 2*0=2,2*1=0,2*2=2.\n\nWe need to test Eq1.\n\nWe could attempt to see if Eq1 holds. Let\'s compute using brute reasoning maybe.\n\nWe need to verify for all x,y,z.\n\nWe can attempt to compute RHS expression stepwise.\n\nFirst compute y*y.\n\n- If y=0: 0*0=0.\n- y=1: 1*1=1.\n- y=2: 2*2=2.\n\nSo y*y = y (idempotent). Good.\n\nThen compute x * (y*y) = x * y.\n\nWe need table for x*y.\n\nLet\'s list x*y for all combos:\n\nx=0: 0*y =0 for any y.\n\nx=1: 1*0=1, 1*1=1, 1*2=0.\n\nx=2: 2*0=2, 2*1=0,